  "notes": "A formal word used in official contexts as well as in technology (push notifications). The noun form {通知|つうち} is very common in both traditional and modern digital contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {通知|つうち}{書|しょ}: notice, notification letter\n- {通知|つうち}{表|ひょう}: report card (school)\n- プッシュ{通知|つうち}: push notification\n- {事前|じぜん}{通知|つうち}: advance notice\n- {通知|つうち}{設定|せってい}: notification settings\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {知|し}らせる: to inform, to let know — everyday native Japanese word\n- {通知|つうち}する: to notify — formal, used for official or systematic notifications\n- {連絡|れんらく}する: to contact — broader, includes any kind of getting in touch",
